ift among Utah's conservative voters, or consolidation of independent and libertarian votes behind Owen, could narrow what polls currently show as a wide margin.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; fundamentals point clearly one way (post-redistricting), so it is treated as safe for that party."]}, "overview": "Utah's 1st District is an open seat after redistricting, and the fundamentals favor Democrats strongly: the district leans Democratic by twelve points, and the national environment adds to that edge. Ben McAdams, a former congressman with name recognition in Utah, has raised $2.7 million and drawn $2.7 million in outside support, while Republican Riley Owen has raised about $150,000 with little outside help.\n\nThe only publicly released poll, from Lighthouse Research in September, showed McAdams leading 63 to 21 among likely voters. Prediction markets on Kalshi and Polymarket put Democratic odds near 97 percent. The candidates have debated as moderates, focusing on prices and artificial intelligence, with little sharp disagreement between them. All available evidence points to a comfortable Democratic win, with the main question being the size of the margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9908, "margin": 20.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9909, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9906, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9886, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9895, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9907, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9979, "margin": 28.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 26.0}, {"date":